From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:59:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Keep the PLL_GPU0 VCO within its range

The A733 manual gives PLL_GPU0 a VCO range of 1.26 GHz to 2.52 GHz
(PLL table), with GPU0PLL = 24 MHz * N / M1 / P0. The driver only limits
N to at least 11, so the rate search can pick a VCO far below the range:
for 1008 MHz it finds N = 42, M1 = 1, P0 = 1 (VCO 1008 MHz) before the
in-range N = 84, P0 = 2 (VCO 2016 MHz).

Limit N to 53..105 and keep the input divider M1 at 1, so every rate the
search returns has its VCO within the documented range. The output
divider P0 (1..8) still covers the rates below the VCO range. The vendor
driver uses the same N range for this PLL and does not use M1 either.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the rate for 1008 MHz
becomes N 84, P0 2, M1 1 (VCO 2016 MHz), locked, with pll-gpu0 and the
GPU core clock reporting 1008 MHz.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index f175d402b936..3b0cfe593cec 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -237,9 +237,13 @@ static CLK_FIXED_FACTOR_HWS(pll_periph1_160M_clk, "pll-periph1-160M",
 static struct ccu_nkmp pll_gpu0_clk = {
 	.enable		= BIT(27),
 	.lock		= BIT(28),
-	.n		= _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_MIN(8, 8, 11),
+	/*
+	 * The VCO (24 MHz * N / M1) must stay within 1.26 GHz to 2.52 GHz:
+	 * keep M1 at 1 and N within 53 to 105.
+	 */
+	.n		= _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_OFFSET_MIN_MAX(8, 8, 1, 53, 105),
 	.m		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(20, 3), /* output divider */
-	.p		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(1, 1), /* input divider */
+	.p		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV_MAX(1, 1, 1), /* input divider */
 	.common		= {
 		.reg		= SUN60I_A733_PLL_GPU_REG,
 		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS_HW("pll-gpu0", pll_ref_hws,
